<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2016/Lupine-Meadow-9x12.jpg" alt="Lupine Meadow. 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2016" width="550" height="418" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Lupine Meadow. 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This is another painting that I've done from one of the "sketch marathon" set of studies. I put this one off for a while as I wanted to work on something larger that I thought would be more interesting. However, that one turned out to be a scraper while this one proved to be much more demanding than I expected.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Unlike the <a href="http://www.portraitsbysimonbland.com/blog/post/north-bluff-from-a-study" target="_blank">previous painting</a> that I posted, I made a few structural and cosmetic changes to the design. &nbsp;There wasn't enough happening in the 5x7 to make it work in a larger size.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I'm not 100% sure that it is finished yet. One of the benefits of photographing and blogging your paintings is that you get to see them in a different context and scale. I made a few changes since first posting this painting (the image shown here is the latest version), but I think the trees would benefit from some additional work.</p>